
# 📘 Pronoun Rules (SSC CGL के लिए महत्वपूर्ण)

### 🔹 Rule 1: Pronoun का Number और Gender Noun के अनुसार होना चाहिए।

✔ Example:

* Every boy must bring **his** book.
  ❌ Wrong: Every boy must bring **their** book.

---

### 🔹 Rule 2: जब दो या अधिक Singular Nouns **and** से जुड़े हों → Pronoun **plural** होगा।

✔ Ram and Shyam are friends. **They** play cricket.

---

### 🔹 Rule 3: अगर दो Nouns **and** से जुड़े हों लेकिन **एक ही व्यक्ति** को दर्शाते हों → Pronoun singular होगा।

✔ The poet and philosopher is dead. **He** was great.

---

### 🔹 Rule 4: Either, Neither, Each, Every, Anyone, Someone, No one → हमेशा **singular pronoun** लेंगे।

✔ **Each of the students has done his duty.**

---

### 🔹 Rule 5: If pronouns of different persons come together → Order will be **2, 3, 1 (231 Rule)**

👉 Second person (You) → Third person (He/She/They) → First person (I/We)
✔ Example: You, he and I are friends.

---

### 🔹 Rule 6: If confession/mistake is shown → Order will be **1, 2, 3 (123 Rule)**

✔ Example: I, you and he are responsible.

---

### 🔹 Rule 7: Reflexive pronouns का प्रयोग तभी होगा जब क्रिया का प्रभाव **खुद subject पर पड़े**।

✔ He hurt **himself**.
❌ Wrong: He is **himself** a teacher. (यहाँ emphatic pronoun चाहिए)

---

### 🔹 Rule 8: Relative Pronoun का प्रयोग सही antecedent के अनुसार होगा।

✔ This is the boy **who** won the prize. (for person)
✔ This is the book **which** I like. (for thing)

---

### 🔹 Rule 9: Pronoun का Case (Subjective / Objective) ध्यान रखना चाहिए।

✔ It is **I** who am guilty. (not “me”)
✔ Let **him** go. (not “he”)

---

# 🎯 Error Detection Questions (Pronoun – SSC CGL Practice)

### ❓ Directions:

निम्नलिखित वाक्यों में error ढूँढें।

---

**Q1.** Everyone should do **their** duty.
**Q2.** Neither of the girls brought **their** book.
**Q3.** One must finish **his** work in time.
**Q4.** Ram and Shyam are brothers. **He** is very intelligent.
**Q5.** This is the only one of my friends **who have** helped me.
**Q6.** It is **me** who is to blame.
**Q7.** Each of the boys in the class must do **their** homework.
**Q8.** I and you will manage it between **ourselves**.
**Q9.** You and he should complete the work between **himself**.
**Q10.** Either of the two boys can give **their** presentation.

---

# 📘 Answer Key + Explanation

**Q1.** ❌ their → ✅ his/her (everyone = singular)
**Q2.** ❌ their → ✅ her (neither = singular)
**Q3.** ✅ Correct (one = singular, his work = correct)
**Q4.** ❌ He → ✅ They (Ram and Shyam = plural)
**Q5.** ❌ have → ✅ has (one of my friends who **has**)
**Q6.** ❌ me → ✅ I (It is I)
**Q7.** ❌ their → ✅ his (each = singular)
**Q8.** ✅ Correct (I and you → ourselves)
**Q9.** ❌ himself → ✅ yourselves (you and he = plural)
**Q10.** ❌ their → ✅ his (either = singular)

---



बहुत बढ़िया 👍 अब मैं आपको **Pronoun Rules का शॉर्टकट Chart** दे रहा हूँ, जिससे आप SSC CGL जैसे एग्ज़ाम में Direct Errors पकड़ सकें।

---

# 📑 **Pronoun Rules (Shortcut Chart)**

### ✅ Rule 1: Subject और Object Case

* Subject → **I, We, He, She, They, Who**
* Object → **Me, Us, Him, Her, Them, Whom**
  👉 Example: *She helped me.* (not *I*)

---

### ✅ Rule 2: Preposition के बाद हमेशा Objective Case

👉 Example: *Between you and me* (not *I*)

---

### ✅ Rule 3: Reflexive Pronoun

* जब Subject और Object एक ही हों → Reflexive लगेगा।
  👉 *He hurt himself.* (not *hisself*)

---

### ✅ Rule 4: Each, Either, Neither, Everyone, Anybody आदि → हमेशा Singular Pronoun लेते हैं।

👉 *Each boy has done his homework.*

---

### ✅ Rule 5: Neither…nor / Either…or → Verb और Pronoun nearest Subject से agree करेंगे।

👉 *Neither Ravi nor his friends confessed that they were guilty.*

---

### ✅ Rule 6: Possessive Pronoun

* **Its** = Possessive (उसका)
* **It’s** = It is / It has
  👉 *The dog wagged its tail.* (not *it’s*)

---

### ✅ Rule 7: Who vs Whom

* **Who** → Subject
* **Whom** → Object
  👉 *Who is knocking?*
  👉 *Whom do you want to meet?*

---

### ✅ Rule 8: Relative Pronouns

* Person → **Who / Whom / Whose**
* Thing → **Which / That**
  👉 *The man who came here is my uncle.*
  👉 *This is the book which I bought.*

---

### ✅ Rule 9: Reciprocal Pronouns

* दो के लिए → **each other**
* दो से अधिक के लिए → **one another**

---

### ✅ Rule 10: Pronoun Consistency

* एक ही वाक्य में Pronoun person न बदले।
  👉 Wrong: *One should take care of his health.*
  👉 Right: *One should take care of one’s health.*

---

📌 यह चार्ट रट लो — Pronoun के Errors आसानी से पकड़ लोगे।

क्या आप चाहेंगे कि मैं इन Rules को **MCQ-based Practice Set (20 Questions)** बना दूँ, ताकि Exam Pattern के हिसाब से प्रैक्टिस हो?
